 "about": "The Caravan Ground's ground (M2 sprint 9, step 1), written by tools/town/caravan_ground.py. `lanes`: the Caravan Ramp R-03 (GAR-11): from R-01's end past the south pavilion's front to its head, the six legs fitted to the ground falling at 13% (the last at the ground's own rate onto the fan), the five switchbacks' level landings, the run-out towards the camp's middle, for tools/terrain/pads.py, tools/town/walls.py, tools/terrain/control.py and the street graph; `path` its line from R-01's end to the camp (x, y and the design's height), round each landing through its middle. `pads`: the camp's yards and houses at the median of their ground (a moved one's `at`), `follow`: those on the ground as it is, for pads.py. `walls`: free-standing walls on the ground, their height over it (the corral GAR-09's), for walls.py. `walk`: the route `camp`'s way on from the ramp's foot (tests/terrain/s3.gd). `cv02_block`: where CV-02's herd comes onto the camp (`entry`) and the 62 spots it halts on (x, y, facing; the first in takes the first), for world/herd.gd. `animals`: the camp's beasts' places (x, y, the design's height, facing): CV-02's yak at its hay (`cv02_hay`) or lying down in twos and threes (`cv02_lie`), CV-01's 60 (`cv01`: at its hay, lying, standing), the picket line's mules and ponies and its two mastiffs (`picket`), the hirer's mules in his corral (`corral`), for world/herd.gd and world/camp_animals.gd. `things`: the kit's types world/camp.gd places (`at` x, y and the design's height, `facing` the front's bearing, shown from `from` until `until`, game minutes, or all day; or `after` minutes after CV-02's halt). Regenerated with the terrain.",
